  <div class="sec-desc">Understanding the geometry of each technique prevents the most common errors.</div>

  <div class="tc">
    <h3>Bisecting angle technique</h3>
    <div class="tc-desc">Default for all maxillary teeth and rostral mandibular teeth — used wherever the sensor cannot be parallel to the root.</div>
    <div class="tc-row">
      <div class="diag-solo">
        <svg width="190" height="210" viewBox="0 0 190 210">
          <defs><marker id="bt" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="3" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#0F6E56"></path></marker></defs>
          <line x1="95" y1="28" x2="95" y2="110" stroke="#5DCAA5" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
          <text x="110" y="44" font-size="9" fill="#0F6E56" font-family="Arial">tooth axis</text>
          <line x1="54" y1="110" x2="148" y2="132" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
          <text x="104" y="152" font-size="9" fill="#185FA5" font-family="Arial">sensor</text>
          <line x1="95" y1="110" x2="46" y2="56" stroke="#FAC775" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5,3"></line>
          <text x="16" y="52" font-size="9" fill="#854F0B" font-family="Arial">bisect</text>
          <line x1="22" y1="98" x2="95" y2="110" stroke="#0F6E56" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#bt)"></line>
          <text x="8" y="94" font-size="9" fill="#0F6E56" font-family="Arial">beam</text>
          <text x="95" y="185" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#444" font-family="Arial" font-weight="bold">Aim beam ⊥ to bisecting line</text>
          <text x="95" y="200" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#666" font-family="Arial">Not ⊥ to sensor. Not ⊥ to tooth.</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="tc-rules">
        <h4>How to do it</h4>
        <ul class="tips">
          <li>Visualise the long axis of the tooth (crown tip → root tip)</li>
          <li>Identify the plane of the sensor</li>
          <li>Mentally bisect the angle between them</li>
          <li>Aim the beam perpendicular to that imaginary line</li>
        </ul>
        <h4 style="margin-top:1rem;">Beam too steep → Foreshortening</h4>
        <ul class="tips">
          <li>Teeth appear shorter than real</li>
          <li>Fix: reduce beam angle; pull tube head back</li>
        </ul>
        <h4 style="margin-top:1rem;">Beam too shallow → Elongation</h4>
        <ul class="tips">
          <li>Teeth appear longer than real</li>
          <li>Fix: increase beam angle; tip tube more toward teeth</li>
        </ul>
        <h4 style="margin-top:1rem;">Quick angle reference</h4>
        <ul class="tips">
          <li>Max. incisors: ~60°</li>
          <li>Max. canine (dog): ~60° oblique</li>
          <li>Max. canine (cat): ~45° oblique</li>
          <li>Max. PM: ~45° (dog) / ~30–40° (cat)</li>
          <li>Mand. incisors/canines: ~20–30°</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="tc">
    <h3>Parallel technique</h3>
    <div class="tc-desc">Gold standard — sensor parallel to root, beam perpendicular to both. Only usable for caudal mandibular teeth in dogs.</div>
    <div class="tc-row">
      <div class="diag-solo">
        <svg width="190" height="190" viewBox="0 0 190 190">
          <defs><marker id="pt" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="3" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#0F6E56"></path></marker></defs>
          <rect x="54" y="28" width="12" height="66" rx="3" fill="#d0e8d8" stroke="#5DCAA5" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
          <rect x="74" y="26" width="14" height="68" rx="3" fill="#d0e8d8" stroke="#5DCAA5" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
          <rect x="96" y="24" width="16" height="70" rx="3" fill="#d0e8d8" stroke="#5DCAA5" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
          <rect x="48" y="102" width="82" height="12" rx="3" fill="#B5D4F4" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
          <text x="89" y="111" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8.5" fill="#0C447C" font-family="Arial">sensor</text>
          <line x1="60" y1="5" x2="60" y2="24" stroke="#0F6E56" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#pt)"></line>
          <line x1="81" y1="5" x2="81" y2="22" stroke="#0F6E56" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#pt)"></line>
          <line x1="104" y1="5" x2="104" y2="20" stroke="#0F6E56" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#pt)"></line>
          <rect x="112" y="95" width="9" height="9" fill="none" stroke="#FAC775" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
          <text x="95" y="155" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#444" font-family="Arial" font-weight="bold">Beam 90° to tooth + sensor</text>
          <text x="95" y="170" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#0F6E56" font-family="Arial">Zero distortion — most accurate</text>
          <text x="95" y="184" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#666" font-family="Arial">No angle calculation required</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="tc-rules">
        <h4>Where to use</h4>
        <ul class="tips">
          <li>Mandibular PM and molars in dogs</li>
          <li>Near-parallel for feline mandibular PM/M</li>
        </ul>
        <h4 style="margin-top:1rem;">Why it's better</h4>
        <ul class="tips">
          <li>No bisecting angle mental arithmetic</li>
          <li>Accurate root length representation</li>
          <li>Less operator-dependent error</li>
        </ul>
        <h4 style="margin-top:1rem;">Why not used everywhere</h4>
        <ul class="tips">
          <li>Palate prevents parallel sensor placement for maxillary teeth</li>
          <li>Mandibular symphysis blocks rostral mandibular teeth</li>
          <li>Cat mandible too narrow for true parallel</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="slob">
    <h3>SLOB rule — separating superimposed roots</h3>
    <div class="slob-rule">Same Lingual · Opposite Buccal</div>
    <div class="tc-row" style="margin-top:.75rem;">
      <div style="text-align:center;">
        <svg width="200" height="210" viewBox="0 0 200 210">
          <defs><marker id="sl" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="3" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#0F6E56"></path></marker></defs>
          <ellipse cx="100" cy="34" rx="60" ry="20" fill="#E1F5EE" stroke="#5DCAA5" stroke-width="1.5"></ellipse>
          <text x="100" y="38" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#085041" font-family="Arial">Maxilla cross-section</text>
          <circle cx="72" cy="34" r="8" fill="#B5D4F4" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
          <text x="72" y="38" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#0C447C" font-family="Arial">MB</text>
          <circle cx="100" cy="34" r="8" fill="#B5D4F4" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
          <text x="100" y="38" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#0C447C" font-family="Arial">DB</text>
          <circle cx="132" cy="34" r="8" fill="#d0e8d8" stroke="#5DCAA5" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
          <text x="132" y="38" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#085041" font-family="Arial">P</text>
          <text x="22" y="32" font-size="8" fill="#666" font-family="Arial">Buccal →</text>
          <text x="150" y="32" font-size="8" fill="#666" font-family="Arial">← Ling.</text>
          <line x1="48" y1="82" x2="86" y2="70" stroke="#0F6E56" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#sl)"></line>
          <text x="22" y="90" font-size="8.5" fill="#0F6E56" font-family="Arial">tube mesial</text>
          <line x1="14" y1="112" x2="186" y2="112" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="1"></line>
          <text x="100" y="108" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8.5" fill="#888" font-family="Arial">Resulting radiograph:</text>
          <circle cx="58" cy="136" r="9" fill="#B5D4F4" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
          <text x="58" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#0C447C" font-family="Arial">MB</text>
          <text x="58" y="152" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8" fill="#444" font-family="Arial">→ mesial</text>
          <circle cx="100" cy="136" r="9" fill="#B5D4F4" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
          <text x="100" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#0C447C" font-family="Arial">DB</text>
          <text x="100" y="152" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8" fill="#444" font-family="Arial">stays</text>
          <circle cx="146" cy="136" r="9" fill="#d0e8d8" stroke="#5DCAA5" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
          <text x="146" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#085041" font-family="Arial">P</text>
          <text x="146" y="152" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8" fill="#444" font-family="Arial">→ distal</text>
          <text x="100" y="180" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#0F6E56" font-family="Arial" font-weight="bold">Roots now separated ✓</text>
          <text x="100" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8.5" fill="#666" font-family="Arial">Compare two images to ID each root</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="slob-desc">
        <p style="margin-bottom:.75rem;">When the tube is moved <strong>mesially</strong>:</p>
        <ul class="tips" style="color:var(--teal-600)">
          <li>Buccal root moves in the <strong>same</strong> direction as the tube → mesially</li>
          <li>Lingual/palatal root moves <strong>opposite</strong> → distally</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin:.75rem 0;">Used for:</p>
        <ul class="tips" style="color:var(--teal-600)">
          <li>Upper 4th PM in dogs (108/208) — separates MB, DB and palatal</li>
          <li>Upper molar in cats (109/209)</li>
          <li>Any multi-rooted tooth with superimposed roots</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top:.75rem;font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.6;"><strong>In practice:</strong> take standard view first. Note which roots overlap. Shift tube mesially 15–20°. Retake. Compare both images side by side to identify each root. Don't shift more than 20° or you introduce elongation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===== ERRORS ===== -->
<div class="section" id="tab-errors">
  <div class="sec-label">Quality control</div>
  <div class="sec-title">Common errors &amp; fixes</div>
  <div class="sec-desc">Most radiograph errors fall into a handful of repeatable patterns. Recognising them quickly means faster retakes and less anaesthetic time.</div>

  <div class="err-grid">
    <div class="err-card">
      <div class="err-head"><div class="err-icon" style="background:var(--red-50)"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18"><path d="M9 2 L9 12" stroke="#A32D2D" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path><circle cx="9" cy="15.5" r="1.5" fill="#A32D2D"></circle></svg></div><div class="err-name">Foreshortening</div></div>
      <div class="err-body">
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Looks like</div><div>Teeth appear shorter — roots look stubby</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Cause</div><div>Beam too steep (overangulated)</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Fix</div><div class="fix">Reduce beam angle — tilt tube away / raise head</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Tip</div><div>Most common with maxillary incisors</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="err-card">
      <div class="err-head"><div class="err-icon" style="background:var(--amber-50)"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18"><path d="M9 2 L9 14" stroke="#854F0B" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M6 14 L12 14" stroke="#854F0B" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></div><div class="err-name">Elongation</div></div>
      <div class="err-body">
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Looks like</div><div>Teeth appear longer — roots stretch</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Cause</div><div>Beam too shallow (underangulated)</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Fix</div><div class="fix">Increase beam angle — tip tube more toward teeth</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Tip</div><div>Common when hesitating to use steep angles over the nose</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="err-card">
      <div class="err-head"><div class="err-icon" style="background:var(--blue-50)"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18"><rect x="3" y="5" width="12" height="9" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.8"></rect><path d="M8 5 L10 5 L10 3 L8 3 Z" fill="#185FA5"></path></svg></div><div class="err-name">Cone cut</div></div>
      <div class="err-body">
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Looks like</div><div>White crescent cutting across corner of image</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Cause</div><div>Beam not centred over sensor</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Fix</div><div class="fix">Centre beam over middle of sensor before exposing</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Tip</div><div>Touch sensor centre as a guide, then position tube over it</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="err-card">
      <div class="err-head"><div class="err-icon" style="background:var(--coral-50)"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18"><path d="M4 9 Q9 3 14 9 Q9 15 4 9Z" fill="none" stroke="#993C1D" stroke-width="1.8"></path></svg></div><div class="err-name">Superimposition</div></div>
      <div class="err-body">
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Looks like</div><div>Roots overlap; cannot distinguish individual roots</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Cause</div><div>Not enough oblique angle; roots aligned with beam</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Fix</div><div class="fix">Add lateral oblique; use SLOB for multi-rooted teeth</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Tip</div><div>Compare two images with tube shifted mesially/distally</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="err-card">
      <div class="err-head"><div class="err-icon" style="background:var(--red-50)"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18"><path d="M3 3 L15 15 M15 3 L3 15" stroke="#A32D2D" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></div><div class="err-name">Motion blur</div></div>
      <div class="err-body">
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Looks like</div><div>Double edges; margins indistinct; ghosting</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Cause</div><div>Patient movement; sensor shift; unsecured tube head</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Fix</div><div class="fix">Check anaesthetic depth; secure sensor; lock tube head</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Tip</div><div>Place sensor on stable foam, not directly on table</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="err-card">
      <div class="err-head"><div class="err-icon" style="background:var(--amber-50)"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18"><circle cx="9" cy="9" r="6.5" fill="none" stroke="#854F0B" stroke-width="1.8"></circle><path d="M9 6 L9 10" stroke="#854F0B" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"></path><circle cx="9" cy="12.5" r="1" fill="#854F0B"></circle></svg></div><div class="err-name">Flipped / mirrored</div></div>
      <div class="err-body">
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Looks like</div><div>Image mirrored; teeth on wrong side</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Cause</div><div>Sensor placed back-to-front; software flip</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Fix</div><div class="fix">Dotted/pimple side always faces beam; check software</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Tip</div><div>Label R/L immediately after every image</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="err-card">
      <div class="err-head"><div class="err-icon" style="background:var(--blue-50)"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18"><circle cx="9" cy="9" r="7" fill="none" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.8"></circle><path d="M9 5 L9 9 L12 12" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></div><div class="err-name">Root tip cut off</div></div>
      <div class="err-body">
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Looks like</div><div>Apex not visible; root truncated at sensor edge</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Cause</div><div>Sensor not positioned far enough apically</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Fix</div><div class="fix">Push sensor further apically; use largest sensor available</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Tip</div><div>Always include 3mm beyond apex</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="err-card">
      <div class="err-head"><div class="err-icon" style="background:var(--coral-50)"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18"><rect x="3" y="3" width="12" height="12" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="#993C1D" stroke-width="1.8"></rect><path d="M3 7 L15 7" stroke="#993C1D" stroke-width="1.2"></path></svg></div><div class="err-name">Overexposed / dark</div></div>
      <div class="err-body">
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Looks like</div><div>Image too dark; tooth detail lost</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Cause</div><div>kVp or exposure time too high; cat on dog settings</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Fix</div><div class="fix">Reduce exposure time 20% or reduce kVp by 5</div></div>
        <div class="err-row"><div class="err-lbl">Tip</div><div>Create size-based presets — cats need far lower settings</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="checklist" style="margin-top:2rem;">
    <div class="checklist-label">Pre-acceptance checklist — run through this before accepting each image</div>
    <div class="checklist-grid">
      <div>☐ &nbsp;Full root length visible?</div>
      <div>☐ &nbsp;All roots separated?</div>
      <div>☐ &nbsp;≥3mm beyond apex?</div>
      <div>☐ &nbsp;Realistic tooth length?</div>
      <div>☐ &nbsp;Image sharp — no blur?</div>
      <div>☐ &nbsp;L/R labelling correct?</div>
      <div>☐ &nbsp;Good contrast?</div>
      <div>☐ &nbsp;No cone cut?</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

